  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Trump administration asks Washington to set aside hundreds of ballots from suspected noncitizen voters",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/26/trump-washington-ballots-aside-noncitizen-voters",
      "description": "<p>This is the latest sign of the administration’s attempts to challenge states with competitive midterm races that could determine control of Congress</p><p>The Trump administration on Monday asked Washington state to set aside any ballots received from more than 400 people it alleges are registered to vote without US citizenship, less than two weeks after making a similar demand in California.</p><p>The announcement is the latest sign of the administration’s attempts to sow doubts about the election or its outcome in states with races that will help determine control of the US Senate and House.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/26/trump-washington-ballots-aside-noncitizen-voters\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-27T01:26:57"
    },
    {
      "title": "Court blocks bid by Trump DoJ to stop California from counting mail-in ballots",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/26/court-california-ballots",
      "description": "<p>Newsom accuses Trump of ‘assault on democracy’ as DoJ claims 20,000 registered voters in state are non-citizens</p><p>A US federal appeals court rejected the Trump administration’s move to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/20/doj-non-citizens-la\">block California</a> from counting the ballots of 20,000 registered voters that the justice department claims are non-citizens.</p><p>The court on Monday ruled 2-1 against Donald ⁠Trump’s ​justice department in the dispute, denying the administration’s demand that election officials segregate the thousands of ballots until people on the list could verify their citizenship. The justice department had given the California secretary of state 48-hours to carry out the order, which state election officials refused – leading to the lawsuit.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/26/court-california-ballots\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-27T00:31:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "US court rules against Trump administration in California voting case",
